{"id": "unknown-2026-06-01-009", "date": "2026-06-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North India cotton yarn prices stable, cotton ease on duty cut", "content": "North India’s cotton yarn market remained stable despite weak demand and the temporary removal of cotton import duty.\nSpinning mills maintained yarn prices, supported by healthy export orders, while local buying stayed cautious.\nCotton prices fell by ₹50-100 per maund amid expectations of higher imports and subdued mill demand, although recycled yarn prices in Panipat remained steady.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-india-cotton-yarn-prices-stable-cotton-ease-on-duty-cut-310691-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-01-010", "date": "2026-06-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India-Oman CEPA comes into force today", "content": "The India-Oman Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement comes into force beginning today and is expected to boost merchandise exports from India. \nIndian exporters now have duty-free access across 98.08 per cent of Oman's tariff lines. \nThe pact will benefit India's labour-intensive sectors like textiles and apparel, leather and footwear.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-oman-cepa-comes-into-force-today-310677-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-01-011", "date": "2026-06-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian polyester raw materials see mixed trend; VSF prices rise", "content": "India’s polyester raw material market showed mixed trends this week, with PTA prices falling and MEG rebounding.\nDespite feedstock volatility, PSF producers kept prices unchanged for the current fortnight.\nDomestic VSF producers raised prices by up to ₹10 per kg on stronger demand and higher costs.\nMarket sentiment remained influenced by crude oil trends and developments in the polyester value chain.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indian-polyester-raw-materials-see-mixed-trend-vsf-prices-rise-310673-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-01-012", "date": "2026-06-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Turkiye’s apparel export decline moderated in January-April 2026", "content": "Türkiye’s apparel exports declined 1.98 per cent year on year to $5.192 billion in January–April 2026 due to weak demand in Europe and rising competition from lower-cost Asian suppliers including Bangladesh, Vietnam and Pakistan.\nHowever, exports rebounded sharply in April, rising 16.2 per cent on the back of seasonal orders and European restocking demand.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/turkiye-s-apparel-export-decline-moderated-in-january-april-2026-310609-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-01-013", "date": "2026-06-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Decoding Indonesia’s evolving export strategy", "content": "Indonesia is gearing up to navigate mounting global uncertainties and reduce its reliance on select markets by pursuing export diversification, forging strategic trade partnerships, and deepening engagement with high-potential export destinations. \nThe country is positioning strategic trade diplomacy alongside manufacturing strength as key to sustaining future export growth.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/decoding-indonesia-s-evolving-export-strategy-310660-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
